  run2 run cce00c: lab01; contain [1,2,3], contain_allow [[1,3],[3,1]], rules CUI->tag CUI, FCI->tag FCI
  run2 FAIL MOVE CUI/sub-cce00c -> CUI/sub-cce00c-renamed allowed and tagged (HTTP 500; tags {'in-sub.txt': [], 'deep/mv.txt': []})
  run2 CONTROL folder rename in Operations (no rule, not contained): HTTP 500
  run2 FAIL MOVE CUI/sub-cce00c-copy -> Archive/dir-cce00c allowed and tagged (HTTP 500; tags {'in-sub.txt': [], 'deep/mv.txt': []})
  run2 DELETE a CUI folder with a file: HTTP 500
  run2 FAIL trash restore of a CUI folder: its file tagged (HTTP None; tags ['CUI'])
  run2 main cce00c: 3 FAIL
  FINDING A (upstream, FIPS): every MOVE/rename/DELETE of a folder WITH CONTENTS answers 500, in any folder (Operations too):
    lib/private/Files/Cache/Cache.php:826 moveFromCache sets the children's path_hash = MD5(...) in SQL, and
    PostgreSQL in FIPS mode refuses: 'ERROR: could not compute MD5 hash: unsupported'. The files are already moved
    on disk, so cache and disk diverge: CUI/sub-cce00c (fileid 336, tagged) stayed in the cache while the data sat at
    CUI/sub-cce00c-renamed, re-scanned as NEW entries 340/342 with NO tag; CUI -> Archive folder move left Archive/dir-cce00c
    untagged (Archive has no rule, so chp:foldertag:check did not even see it); a CUI folder DELETE moved the data to
    __groupfolders/1/trash on disk while the folder still listed in CUI.
    Same failure for a single FILE with old versions moved to another team folder: groupfolders
    VersionsBackend::moveVersionsBetweenFolders moves versions/<fileid> (a folder) -> MD5 -> 500.
  FINDING B (bypass): a WebDAV MOVE of a trash item straight to files/lab01/Operations/... answered 201 and created an
    UNTAGGED copy of the deleted CUI file in Operations (Sabre falls back to copy+delete, a create the ContainListener
    never sees). Same for an old version.
  FIX in 1.0 (final): DavGuardListener (SabrePluginAddEvent: beforeMove/beforeCopy from trashbin/ or versions/ to files/ -> 403)
    and FolderGuardListener (while SELECT MD5() fails: refuse move/delete of a non-empty folder and the cross-folder move
    of a file with old versions, before anything moves). The real fix (MD5 in the database) is open, see the Task 3 report.
  HTTP 412 in run 1: test artefact (the script sent 'Overwrite: F' to the restore endpoints; removed).
  version restore failures in runs 1-2: test artefact (two PUTs in the same second = one version); the script now waits 1.5 s.

